    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you into the clinic today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, doctor, my wife sent me down here. It's... it's about the men at the domino table. We play down at the center. Mostly just draw dominoes, you know. I used to play with my brother a lot before he passed back in '98. We'd sit out on the porch for hours. \n\nBut lately, the men there, they've been giving these little messages. Just meant for me. And the radio announcer does it too. I got one of those little radios I keep out in the garage... bought it at Sears a long, long time ago. Still works fine, you just have to wiggle the dial a bit to get the static out. \n\nBut anyway, the announcer and the domino men, they slip in these messages. And even when my wife says it is just talk—she's always fussing about something, she was just fussing about me leaving the garden hose out this morning—but I know what I hear. I know they are warning me to be careful. That's why I came in.",
