    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "When you mention hearing voices, do you hear them speaking even when the radio is off and nobody is around?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Well, yes, I suppose I do. Some afternoons, when the house is just dead quiet... you know, my wife goes down to her sister's on Tuesdays to help with the quilting, they've been making this big star pattern quilt for the church auction. Beautiful thing, all blues and yellows. Her sister's got that big sunroom on the back of her house, gets real hot in the summer though. But anyway, when she's gone and it's quiet, I'll be sitting there and I'll hear my old friend call my name right from the porch. Or sometimes he's humming one of those old choir songs we used to sing. Clear as day, like he's standing right there next to the rocking chair. That rocking chair needs fixing, actually. One of the spindles came loose when my grandson was visiting last Easter. Boy was climbing all over it like a monkey. I told him to get down, but you know how kids are nowadays, they just don't listen. They've got their faces stuck in those little screens all the time. Can't even have a decent conversation with 'em.",
