    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have you noticed any difficulties with your memory recently?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Memory? No, I haven't noticed any trouble with that. My memory's sharp as a tack, mostly. I mean, just yesterday I remembered to pick up the exact brand of coffee my wife likes from the grocery store without her even having to write it down. Maxwell House, the blue tin. \n\nThough, I'll tell you, they went and moved everything around at the store again. Drives me absolutely up the wall when they do that. The manager there, young fella named Tim—wears these thick glasses, looks like he's about twelve years old, honestly—he moved all the canned peaches all the way over to aisle four. Took me a good ten minutes to find them. I used to buy those exact same peaches for my mother back when she was living over on Elm Street. She had this little yellow house with a big old oak tree out front. Dropped acorns all over the driveway, sounded like hail when you drove over 'em in the winter. We used to have to sweep them up every Sunday before church, otherwise folks would twist an ankle walking up to the door. Pastor Miller came over once and nearly went flying. He was a good preacher, though. Spoke real loud, you never fell asleep in his pews.",
