      "doctor_question": "Do you have any medical conditions or physical health problems that you are currently being treated for?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Medical problems? No, sir, I don't have anything like that I'm seeing a doctor for. I've always had a real strong constitution, you know? Never needed much doctoring at all. My granddaddy always said a raw clove of garlic and a good night's sleep would keep the sickness away. He used to grow his own garlic out behind the old tractor shed. Biggest bulbs you ever did see. He'd string 'em up right there in the kitchen, smelled to high heaven, but my grandma never complained. She was an absolute saint, that woman. Used to bake these wild blackberry pies... we'd go picking down by the old creek bed, get our arms scratched up something awful by the brambles, but Lord it was worth it. You just can't find blackberries like that anymore. The ones in the store are all watery, got no taste to 'em. Same with the tomatoes, honestly. Look red enough, but you bite into 'em and they taste just like wet cardboard.",
